{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15426194","formula":"C₁₂H₆Br₄O₂","hill":"C12H6Br4O2","elements":["H","C","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":6.0,"O":2.0,"Br":4.0},"names":{"en":"Bromophene"},"descriptions":{"en":"Bromophene (MC21-A or C58) is a bactericidal antibiotic first isolated from the O-BC30 strain of a marine bacterium, Pseudoalteromonas phenolica. A 2024 study reported that bromophene exhibited antibacterial activity against methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA), with a minimum inhibitory concentration of 2 μg/mL against 39 different isolates. In the same study, bromophene exhibited in vitro antibacterial activity comparable to or greater than that of daptomycin, vancomycin, and linezolid under the conditions tested."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":30891,"mass":501.79,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=C(C=C(C(=C1C2=C(C(=CC(=C2)Br)Br)O)O)Br)Br","inchikey":"TXODBIOSWNNKJM-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2,4-dibromo-6-(3,5-dibromo-2-hydroxyphenyl)phenol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"30891","atoms":24,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.892,"y":1.879,"z":1.794,"el":"Br"},{"x":-3.892,"y":-1.879,"z":1.795,"el":"Br"},{"x":3.667,"y":-2.129,"z":-2.214,"el":"Br"},{"x":-3.667,"y":2.129,"z":-2.215,"el":"Br"},{"x":0.812,"y":1.672,"z":1.521,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.812,"y":-1.672,"z":1.522,"el":"O"},{"x":0.725,"y":-0.016,"z":-0.166,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.725,"y":0.016,"z":-0.166,"el":"C"},{"x":1.461,"y":0.814,"z":0.679,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.461,"y":-0.814,"z":0.679,"el":"C"},{"x":1.382,"y":-0.893,"z":-1.029,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.382,"y":0.893,"z":-1.029,"el":"C"},{"x":2.855,"y":0.767,"z":0.662,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.855,"y":-0.767,"z":0.662,"el":"C"},{"x":2.776,"y":-0.94,"z":-1.046,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.776,"y":0.94,"z":-1.046,"el":"C"},{"x":3.512,"y":-0.11,"z":-0.201,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.512,"y":0